(
K05 / C5 (2026-10-07): contact_target_geometry_switch (manual
Professional 6.107) is the Professional name of
contact_geometry_switch. Input contact_target_geometry_index0 with the
switch -yes on index 0: the outward normal of geometry_point 1 turns
to -x, node 2 is on the outward side and flies freely: after one step
x = 0.99 + 0.03 = 1.02 (Professional 02-08-2026 1.02; the GNU name
contact_geometry_switch gives the same).
GNU before: abort "Program error detected for data: contact_geometry.
Data is allocated in a parallel loop" (alias PUT in the parallel loop).
)
echo -no
number_of_space_dimensions 1
materi_velocity
materi_stress
end_initia
mesh -follow_material
node 1  0.
node 2  0.99
element 1  -bar2  1 2
group_type 0  -materi
group_materi_density 0  1.
geometry_point 1  1.3 0.3
node_dof 2  0.03  0. 0. 0. 0. 0. 0.
contact_penalty_velocity  10.
contact_target_geometry 0  -geometry_point 1
contact_target_geometry_switch 0  -yes
timestep_predict_velocity -yes
control_timestep  10  1. 1.
target_item  1  -node 2 0
target_value 1  1.02 1.e-3
end_data
